{"authored" [{"question" "q-40437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{4}6x\\,dy]dA,\n$$\n\nEvaluate the integral above over the right bounded region $D$ in the $xz$-plane: $0\\le x\\le2$ and $0\\le z\\le4-x^2$. Its boundary consists of $z=0$, $x=0$, and $z+x^2=4$, on the nonnegative-$x$ side." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-40437/review.json" "file_sha256" "b5c517ce55d3519e5987679b7736102dde0005d308982857254ccdeabfd56a84" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-40437/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "0bee71f5ff1fbc0b2d3afc08bafb70c926744ddf5a339caf126e2d4299f057a9" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-40437/verification.json" "basis" 2084 "rationale" "Clarify nonnegative-x right lobe explicitly; preserve authentic key64, existing field and answer identities. Original ambiguous prompt and uncertain solver retained."} {"question" "q-40437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The clarified region is the right bounded lobe, $D=\\{(x,z):0\\le x\\le2,0\\le z\\le4-x^2\\}$. Integrate first with respect to $y$:\n\n$$\\int_{x^2}^4 6x\\,dy=6x(4-x^2).$$\n\nThe $z$ interval has length $4-x^2$, so\n\n$$\\iint_D\\left[\\int_{x^2}^4 6x\\,dy\\right]dA=\\int_0^2 6x(4-x^2)^2\\,dx=[-(4-x^2)^3]_0^2=64.$$\n\nAll inner limits are ordered. The original boundary description also encloses a left lobe, $-2\\le x\\le0$, whose integral is $-64$; it did not explicitly select a side of $x=0$. Selecting the right lobe explicitly gives $64$." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-40437/review.json" "file_sha256" "b5c517ce55d3519e5987679b7736102dde0005d308982857254ccdeabfd56a84" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-40437/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "0bee71f5ff1fbc0b2d3afc08bafb70c926744ddf5a339caf126e2d4299f057a9" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-40437/verification.json" "basis" 2084 "rationale" "Clarify nonnegative-x right lobe explicitly; preserve authentic key64, existing field and answer identities. Original ambiguous prompt and uncertain solver retained."} {"question" "q-40437" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "64"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-40437/review.json" "file_sha256" "b5c517ce55d3519e5987679b7736102dde0005d308982857254ccdeabfd56a84" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-40437/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "0bee71f5ff1fbc0b2d3afc08bafb70c926744ddf5a339caf126e2d4299f057a9" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-40437/verification.json" "basis" 2084 "rationale" "Clarify nonnegative-x right lobe explicitly; preserve authentic key64, existing field and answer identities. Original ambiguous prompt and uncertain solver retained."} {"question" "q-40437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{4}6x\\,dy]dA,\n$$\n\nEvaluate the repeated integral above given that $D$ is a region in the $xz$-plane bounded by the lines $z=0,$ $x=0,$ and the curve $z+{x}^{2}=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/state.json" "file_sha256" "788a9691568f64cb7c13aa285ad76c93e87db7b16a06c4ae123e8caa4136a543" "basis" 2077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-40437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{4}6x\\,dy]dA & ={∬}_{D}6x[y]_{y={x}^{2}}^{y=4}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}6x(4-{x}^{2})\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}24x-6{x}^{3}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate this double integral, we plot $D$ as a type I plane region in the $xz$-plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/assets/612c4fda39f7003024c322b6d1fa5c279815923905c8d023547a3be6b4a6805a.png)\n\nTherefore, to evaluate our double integral as a repeated integral over this region, we integrate with respect to $z$ and then with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}24x-6{x}^{3}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-{x}^{2}}24x-6{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(24x-6{x}^{3})[z]_{z=0}^{z=4-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(24x-6{x}^{3})(4-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}96x-48{x}^{3}+6{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[48{x}^{2}-12{x}^{4}+{x}^{6}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(192-192+64)-0 \\\\  & =64\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/state.json" "file_sha256" "788a9691568f64cb7c13aa285ad76c93e87db7b16a06c4ae123e8caa4136a543" "basis" 2077 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-40437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "27b5b7a888138e758a90a755e287632e41cbd828d2